X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96079072816299

Hi all,
    The short answer is that a clone file set of an active Oracle
database is not going to provide a reliable backup.  The 2 ways to get
around this are:
1. Shutdown the database, make the clone file set and start it back up
again.
2. Put the tablespaces into backup mode, and force a checkpoint. Then
follow the brown book on Oracle backup and Recovery.

Thanks to
Guy R. Loucks
Neil McAully
Michael Buchholtz

