I have seen this problem on a PW433au running 4.0D. What is happening =
is
that all of the swap space is being used up. Once the machine runs out =
of
swap space, it will 'freeze' until the process causing the problem =
finishes
or crashes. The 'freeze' is the machine not being able get any free =
memory
pages. You are probably running with strict swap allocation. In =
reality, you
are probably not using any, or much, swap space, but the strict =
allocation
policy will allocate all swap space even though nothing is swapping.

In my situation, it was a very badly behaving X-Window application, =
with a
huge memory requirement, that caused by system to freeze.

