<P><FONT COLOR=3D"#0000FF" SIZE=3D2 FACE=3D"Fixedsys">My original =
question is at the bottom of this message. I was looking for</FONT>
<BR><FONT COLOR=3D"#0000FF" SIZE=3D2 FACE=3D"Fixedsys">a way to =
minimize downtime of our Oracle databases when we perform a cold</FONT>
<BR><FONT COLOR=3D"#0000FF" SIZE=3D2 FACE=3D"Fixedsys">backup. My =
thought was to shutdown the databases, break the existing =
mirrors,</FONT>
<BR><FONT COLOR=3D"#0000FF" SIZE=3D2 FACE=3D"Fixedsys">remount the =
filesystems, startup the databases, and then backup the piece</FONT>
<BR><FONT COLOR=3D"#0000FF" SIZE=3D2 FACE=3D"Fixedsys">of the mirrors =
that was broken off (and then resyncing that piece).</FONT>
</P>

<P><FONT COLOR=3D"#0000FF" SIZE=3D2 FACE=3D"Fixedsys">I heard almost =
immediately from alan@nabeth.cxo.dec.com and had two other</FONT>
<BR><FONT COLOR=3D"#0000FF" SIZE=3D2 FACE=3D"Fixedsys">replies from =
Steve Hancock [hancock@decatl.alf.dec.com], and from</FONT>
<BR><FONT COLOR=3D"#0000FF" SIZE=3D2 FACE=3D"Fixedsys">North, Walter =
[Wnorth@state.mt.us].</FONT>
</P>

<P><FONT COLOR=3D"#0000FF" SIZE=3D2 FACE=3D"Fixedsys">Steve =
wrote:</FONT>
<BR>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <FONT SIZE=3D2 =
FACE=3D"Arial">The procedure looks ok, except that the mount of the =
mirrored plex will</FONT>
<BR>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <FONT SIZE=3D2 =
FACE=3D"Arial">not work as you have stated. The mount will fail, =
because you cannot</FONT>
<BR>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <FONT SIZE=3D2 =
FACE=3D"Arial">have two active domains with the same domain ID. The way =
around this</FONT>
<BR>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <FONT SIZE=3D2 =
FACE=3D"Arial">restriction, in V4.0D and higher, is to use the &quot;-o =
dual&quot; option to</FONT>
<BR>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <FONT SIZE=3D2 =
FACE=3D"Arial">the mount command. If you use this, you will see your =
procedure</FONT>
<BR>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <FONT SIZE=3D2 =
FACE=3D"Arial">work.</FONT>
<BR><FONT COLOR=3D"#0000FF" SIZE=3D2 FACE=3D"Fixedsys">I tried this and =
it works! Woohoo! I don't know if we'll do this or</FONT>
<BR><FONT COLOR=3D"#0000FF" SIZE=3D2 FACE=3D"Fixedsys">not, but I now =
know it's an option.</FONT>
</P>

<P><FONT COLOR=3D"#0000FF" SIZE=3D2 FACE=3D"Fixedsys">Alan suggested =
using cloning and then referred me to the man pages for</FONT>
<BR><FONT COLOR=3D"#0000FF" SIZE=3D2 FACE=3D"Fixedsys">mount (lucky for =
me Steve gave me the option b/4 I had a chance to look).</FONT>
<BR><FONT COLOR=3D"#0000FF" SIZE=3D2 FACE=3D"Fixedsys">I'm not sure =
cloning will work for us, as some of the filesystems are</FONT>
<BR><FONT COLOR=3D"#0000FF" SIZE=3D2 FACE=3D"Fixedsys">higher than 95% =
used. Alan does raise some good points so I'm including</FONT>
<BR><FONT COLOR=3D"#0000FF" SIZE=3D2 FACE=3D"Fixedsys">all 3 of his =
notes here:</FONT>
<BR><FONT COLOR=3D"#0000FF" SIZE=3D2 FACE=3D"Fixedsys">Alan 1:</FONT> =
<FONT SIZE=3D2 FACE=3D"Arial">Have you considered using AdvFS clones =
for the purpose?&nbsp; The</FONT>
<BR>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <FONT SIZE=3D2 =
FACE=3D"Arial">clonefset command creates a read-only snapshot of the =
fileset</FONT>
<BR>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <FONT SIZE=3D2 =
FACE=3D"Arial">metadata.&nbsp; Then as file pages (blocks) are changed, =
the</FONT>
<BR>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <FONT SIZE=3D2 =
FACE=3D"Arial">original is written to the clone so the original is =
kept</FONT>
<BR>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <FONT SIZE=3D2 =
FACE=3D"Arial">as a snapshot.&nbsp; This method saves you the trouble =
breaking</FONT>
<BR>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <FONT SIZE=3D2 =
FACE=3D"Arial">the mirrors (and the associated risk of not having =
mirrored</FONT>
<BR>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <FONT SIZE=3D2 =
FACE=3D"Arial">data) and the copy time to put the mirrors back =
together.</FONT>
</P>

<P>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <FONT SIZE=3D2 =
FACE=3D"Arial">It has the same problem of making the file system =
quiet</FONT>
<BR>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <FONT SIZE=3D2 =
FACE=3D"Arial">enough to get a good backup, but that depends as much =
on</FONT>
<BR>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <FONT SIZE=3D2 =
FACE=3D"Arial">the data as the file system; low risk for a typical =
time-</FONT>
<BR>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <FONT SIZE=3D2 =
FACE=3D"Arial">sharing load off hours, higher risk for a 24 hour =
per</FONT>
<BR>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <FONT SIZE=3D2 =
FACE=3D"Arial">day database.</FONT>
</P>

<P>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <FONT SIZE=3D2 =
FACE=3D"Arial">And, the domain is used for space for the clone.&nbsp; =
If the</FONT>
<BR>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <FONT SIZE=3D2 =
FACE=3D"Arial">domain is fairly full and there are lots of changes =
during</FONT>
<BR>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <FONT SIZE=3D2 =
FACE=3D"Arial">the lifetime of the clone it could run out of =
space.&nbsp; Finally</FONT>
<BR>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <FONT SIZE=3D2 =
FACE=3D"Arial">removing the clone can take a long time in some =
cases.</FONT>
</P>

<P><FONT COLOR=3D"#0000FF" SIZE=3D2 FACE=3D"Fixedsys">Alan 2:</FONT>
<BR>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <FONT SIZE=3D2 =
FACE=3D"Arial">Ah, you already knew about clones.&nbsp; Sort of.&nbsp; =
I hadn't</FONT>
<BR>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <FONT SIZE=3D2 =
FACE=3D"Arial">read all the message.</FONT>
</P>

<P>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <FONT SIZE=3D2 =
FACE=3D"Arial">AdvFS does have domain unique information on its =
volumes,</FONT>
<BR>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <FONT SIZE=3D2 =
FACE=3D"Arial">but there is an option to mount or one of the =
other</FONT>
<BR>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <FONT SIZE=3D2 =
FACE=3D"Arial">domain related commands to have it ignore this =
piece</FONT>
<BR>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <FONT SIZE=3D2 =
FACE=3D"Arial">when you mount it.&nbsp; Check the mount manual page =
first.</FONT>
</P>

<P>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <FONT SIZE=3D2 =
FACE=3D"Arial">The advantage of using AdvFS's cloneing ability is =
that</FONT>
<BR>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <FONT SIZE=3D2 =
FACE=3D"Arial">you don't lose the redundancy of your data during =
the</FONT>
<BR>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <FONT SIZE=3D2 =
FACE=3D"Arial">backup.</FONT>
</P>

<P><FONT COLOR=3D"#0000FF" SIZE=3D2 FACE=3D"Fixedsys">Alan3:</FONT>
<BR>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <FONT SIZE=3D2 =
FACE=3D"Arial">Estimate how much time it will take backup the data =
and</FONT>
<BR>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <FONT SIZE=3D2 =
FACE=3D"Arial">resync the mirrors.&nbsp; That's how long you won't =
have</FONT>
<BR>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <FONT SIZE=3D2 =
FACE=3D"Arial">mirrored data.&nbsp; Get someone in your finance =
department</FONT>
<BR>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <FONT SIZE=3D2 =
FACE=3D"Arial">to calculate how much that risk is worth.&nbsp; Disks =
are cheap</FONT>
<BR>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <FONT SIZE=3D2 =
FACE=3D"Arial">even when you need to buy twice as many to have a =
spare</FONT>
<BR>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <FONT SIZE=3D2 =
FACE=3D"Arial">volume to have enough free space for the clone.</FONT>
</P>
<BR>

<P><FONT COLOR=3D"#0000FF" SIZE=3D2 FACE=3D"Fixedsys">Walt also pointed =
out that I missed a 'volume stop' command.</FONT>
</P>

<P><FONT COLOR=3D"#0000FF" SIZE=3D2 FACE=3D"Fixedsys">Original =
message:</FONT>
<BR><FONT SIZE=3D2 FACE=3D"Arial">8200, 4.0d PK2, ASE, LSM</FONT>
<BR><FONT SIZE=3D2 FACE=3D"Arial">&nbsp;</FONT>
<BR><FONT SIZE=3D2 FACE=3D"Arial">I've got several advanced filesystem =
domains on mirrored LSM volumes</FONT>
<BR><FONT SIZE=3D2 FACE=3D"Arial">that I'd like to backup by breaking =
the mirrors, doing a vdump,</FONT>
<BR><FONT SIZE=3D2 FACE=3D"Arial">and then reattaching the removed plex =
for resyncing. Something along</FONT>
<BR><FONT SIZE=3D2 FACE=3D"Arial">the lines of:</FONT>
<BR><FONT SIZE=3D2 FACE=3D"Arial">&nbsp;&nbsp; umount =
/filesystem</FONT>
<BR><FONT SIZE=3D2 FACE=3D"Arial">&nbsp;&nbsp; volplex dis plex2</FONT>
<BR><FONT SIZE=3D2 FACE=3D"Arial">&nbsp;&nbsp; mount /filesystem</FONT>
<BR><FONT SIZE=3D2 FACE=3D"Arial">&nbsp;&nbsp; volmake -Ufsgen vol =
backup plex2</FONT>
<BR><FONT SIZE=3D2 FACE=3D"Arial">&nbsp;&nbsp; volume start =
backup</FONT>
<BR><FONT SIZE=3D2 FACE=3D"Arial">Now I'd need to mount the quiescent =
filesystem (if that's possible) and</FONT>
<BR><FONT SIZE=3D2 FACE=3D"Arial">do a vdump, so I think I need =
to:</FONT>
<BR><FONT SIZE=3D2 FACE=3D"Arial">&nbsp;&nbsp; mkdir =
/etc/fdmns/newdomain</FONT>
<BR><FONT SIZE=3D2 FACE=3D"Arial">&nbsp;&nbsp; ln -s =
/dev/vol/rootdg/backup /etc/fdmns/newdomain/backup</FONT>
<BR><FONT SIZE=3D2 FACE=3D"Arial">&nbsp;&nbsp; mount =
newdomain#oldfilesetname /mnt</FONT>
<BR><FONT SIZE=3D2 FACE=3D"Arial">If that works, then I'd issue a vdump =
command followed by:</FONT>
<BR><FONT SIZE=3D2 FACE=3D"Arial">&nbsp;&nbsp; volplex -f dis =
plex2</FONT>
<BR><FONT SIZE=3D2 FACE=3D"Arial">[should have a 'volume stop backup' =
command here that was missing from the original note]</FONT>
<BR><FONT SIZE=3D2 FACE=3D"Arial">&nbsp;&nbsp; voledit rm backup</FONT>
<BR><FONT SIZE=3D2 FACE=3D"Arial">&nbsp;&nbsp; volplex att =
original_volume plex2</FONT>
<BR><FONT SIZE=3D2 FACE=3D"Arial">&nbsp;</FONT>
<BR><FONT SIZE=3D2 FACE=3D"Arial">Does anyone know if this will work? =
DEC recommends using cloning for</FONT>
<BR><FONT SIZE=3D2 FACE=3D"Arial">AdvFS, but with a mirrored volume, =
the clone already exists. I'm not</FONT>
<BR><FONT SIZE=3D2 FACE=3D"Arial">sure what sorts of advfs metadata =
stuff exists on the volumes, whether</FONT>
<BR><FONT SIZE=3D2 FACE=3D"Arial">I can just create a new domain as =
suggested above and have a successful</FONT>
<BR><FONT SIZE=3D2 FACE=3D"Arial">mount. I think someone asked this =
question last month but I didn't</FONT>
<BR><FONT SIZE=3D2 FACE=3D"Arial">see a summary. TIA</FONT>
</P>
<BR>
<BR>
<BR>

