To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: Tru64 Unix 5.0 with HSZ80
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96079072816116

There are two ways to connect the HSZ80 (dual redundant) subsystem to a
computer -- Transparent Failover Mode and Multibus Redundant Mode.

I understand that v5.0 supports Multibus mode (as this mode is OS
dependant).  Transparent mode works like a champ (quite easily too
because all the configuration is done on the HSZ80), but I'm unsure of
what needs to be set up on the OS for Multibus mode.

I (think) that I'd prefer to use multibus mode for load balancing
between the two SCSI buses and it seems to have the same level of
availability as Transparent mode....

--Robert

