Thank to Bob Vicker for your solution. I get the patch from technical
support of digital and installed.
The login from console is correct.

The origal question:

> I have DU 4.0E and use one account for operator named "operador", this
> account login also from the console and execute task administrative with
> sudo utility.
>
> After installed PK2 for DU4.0E, this account not login from console, send
> the message "login incorrecct ; try again". With this same account login
> from another terminal and login correctly.
>
> The same is replicate in another Alpha and use DCE in Console.
>
> What is the problem? Is PK 2?
>

The solution of Bob (R.Vickers@dcs.rhbnc.ac.uk)

There is a bug in 4.0E PK2 which prevents users with 8-character user
names from logging in via X. Your choices are
(a) change to a shorter user name
(b) login by a different means (e.g. telnet)
(c) obtain  patch STLQ74705 from Compaq
(d) upgrade to 4.0F


Marcelo Alonso Mondragon
